From 792c2043b6f678252907b85b067cae050dbfd1be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Spatiand-build <claude@prasetya.id>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 04:48:13 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] Spatiand: built for Android libc: Bluetooth through the
 Spatiand app

Chromium's Linux build reaches Bluetooth through BlueZ on D-Bus, which Android has not got. On Android's libc its adapter is Android's Bluetooth LE instead, reached through the Spatiand app's bridge (android/src/id/prasetya/spatiand/BluetoothBridge.java): an abstract socket, spatiand-bluetooth, for the app's own processes, one JSON object a line each way (device/bluetooth/spatiand). Low energy, central, GATT client: scanning, connecting, services, characteristics and descriptors read and written, notifications; what Web Bluetooth asks for. Web Bluetooth stays as on Linux: behind experimental web platform features, and a site asks only once allowed to (Cromite).
